            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for a jackal, then the Bengali for a bat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: প্যাঁচা",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "প্যাঁচা — pyā̃chā — \"an owl\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "প্যাঁচা (pyā̃chā) (pyāṁchā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from pecaka, \"owl\" (CDIAL 8375)."
            }
